window.CET6_DATA("data/articles/day-059.json",{"day":59,"title":"Who Deserves a Place at the Table?","targetWords":[{"word":"dismay","gloss":"沮丧","context":"The closure of a community kitchen caused dismay across the district.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"indignant","gloss":"愤慨的","context":"A stern official called its shabby building unsafe, while an indignant, restless crowd treated the decision as an outrage.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"outrage","gloss":"愤怒","context":"A stern official called its shabby building unsafe, while an indignant, restless crowd treated the decision as an outrage.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"pardon","gloss":"原谅","context":"One speaker described a homeless man as a dumb troublemaker, and she asked the chair to pardon her interruption before challenging the label.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"pity","gloss":"同情","context":"There was no need to pity him, she argued, if pity meant denying his ability to contribute.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"plea","gloss":"恳求","context":"Volunteers were wary of confronting the council, but a timid cook named Mei made a public plea: repair the building, she asked, rather than abandon the people who depended on it.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"shabby","gloss":"破旧的","context":"A stern official called its shabby building unsafe, while an indignant, restless crowd treated the decision as an outrage.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"stern","gloss":"严厉的","context":"A stern official called its shabby building unsafe, while an indignant, restless crowd treated the decision as an outrage.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"sturdy","gloss":"坚固的","context":"Its sturdy tables had hosted both quiet meals and merry celebrations.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"wary","gloss":"机警的","context":"Volunteers were wary of confronting the council, but a timid cook named Mei made a public plea: repair the building, she asked, rather than abandon the people who depended on it.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"weary","gloss":"疲倦","context":"The kitchen had served people too weary to cook after work and those whose wages barely covered rent.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"zeal","gloss":"热情","context":"Nevertheless, the volunteers returned with renewed zeal.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"compassion","gloss":"同情","context":"Expressions of compassion were easy; practical support was harder.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"ego","gloss":"自我","context":"Her own ego also troubled her: she wanted to win the argument partly because she feared losing a place where people seemed to adore her cooking.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"eloquent","gloss":"雄辩的","context":"An eloquent property developer offered a gorgeous replacement restaurant that most former visitors could never afford.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"farewell","gloss":"告别","context":"Now a small notice announced an immediate farewell.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"grim","gloss":"可怕的","context":"There had been a grim dispute over alcohol and one ruthless attempt to steal donated funds.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"restless","gloss":"不安宁的","context":"A stern official called its shabby building unsafe, while an indignant, restless crowd treated the decision as an outrage.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"scorn","gloss":"轻蔑","context":"She disliked the hypocrisy of praising community spirit while treating poverty with scorn.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"benevolent","gloss":"仁慈的","context":"A benevolent donor proposed emergency funding, but his jealous business partner dismissed the guests as pathetic.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"discreet","gloss":"谨慎的","context":"Mei avoided a hysterical response and presented bills, attendance records, and a discreet account of residents' needs.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"dumb","gloss":"愚蠢的","context":"One speaker described a homeless man as a dumb troublemaker, and she asked the chair to pardon her interruption before challenging the label.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"gorgeous","gloss":"华丽的","context":"An eloquent property developer offered a gorgeous replacement restaurant that most former visitors could never afford.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"jealous","gloss":"嫉妒的","context":"A benevolent donor proposed emergency funding, but his jealous business partner dismissed the guests as pathetic.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"merry","gloss":"愉快的","context":"Its sturdy tables had hosted both quiet meals and merry celebrations.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"timid","gloss":"胆怯的","context":"Volunteers were wary of confronting the council, but a timid cook named Mei made a public plea: repair the building, she asked, rather than abandon the people who depended on it.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"amaze","gloss":"吃惊","context":"Such accounts could amaze officials accustomed to statistics, but Mei refused to claim that the service was flawless.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"bewilder","gloss":"使迷惑","context":"At a hearing, the council chair adopted a cordial manner but asked questions that seemed designed to bewilder the volunteers.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"hypocrisy","gloss":"伪善","context":"She disliked the hypocrisy of praising community spirit while treating poverty with scorn.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"jolly","gloss":"快乐的","context":"It was not a jolly ending to every difficulty, and a careless headline might still appal someone looking only for scandal.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"numb","gloss":"麻木的","context":"Mei felt numb at this contrast.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"pathetic","gloss":"可怜的","context":"A benevolent donor proposed emergency funding, but his jealous business partner dismissed the guests as pathetic.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"adore","gloss":"热爱","context":"Her own ego also troubled her: she wanted to win the argument partly because she feared losing a place where people seemed to adore her cooking.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"amiable","gloss":"亲切的","context":"The testimony included an amiable retired nurse who called her husband darling even after forty years of marriage.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"anguish","gloss":"痛苦","context":"She explained how shared dinners had eased her anguish following his illness.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"appal","gloss":"吓坏","context":"It was not a jolly ending to every difficulty, and a careless headline might still appal someone looking only for scandal.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"cordial","gloss":"热忱的","context":"At a hearing, the council chair adopted a cordial manner but asked questions that seemed designed to bewilder the volunteers.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"darling","gloss":"亲爱的","context":"The testimony included an amiable retired nurse who called her husband darling even after forty years of marriage.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"fright","gloss":"惊恐","context":"Another visitor described the fright of entering the kitchen alone, followed by relief when someone welcomed him.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"idiot","gloss":"白痴","context":"Calling an opponent an idiot might offer brief satisfaction, but listening could reveal that even hostile parties wanted a safer district.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"intercourse","gloss":"性行为","context":"The kitchen also hosted a nurse who explained sexual health, including the risks of unprotected intercourse.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"riddle","gloss":"谜","context":"Mei understood that a community was not a riddle solved by separating admirable people from everyone else.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"ruthless","gloss":"无情的","context":"There had been a grim dispute over alcohol and one ruthless attempt to steal donated funds.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"cunning","gloss":"狡猾的","context":"Honest discussion, rather than cunning publicity, was essential to trust.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"hysterical","gloss":"歇斯底里的","context":"Mei avoided a hysterical response and presented bills, attendance records, and a discreet account of residents' needs.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"naughty","gloss":"淘气的","context":"Nor should a naughty child at dinner be treated like a wicked enemy.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"wicked","gloss":"邪恶的","context":"Nor should a naughty child at dinner be treated like a wicked enemy.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"the","gloss":"这；该","context":"The closure of a community kitchen caused dismay across the district.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"a","gloss":"一个","context":"The closure of a community kitchen caused dismay across the district.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"that","gloss":"那个","context":"An eloquent property developer offered a gorgeous replacement restaurant that most former visitors could never afford.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null}],"paragraphs":[{"en":"The closure of a community kitchen caused dismay across the district. A stern official called its shabby building unsafe, while an indignant, restless crowd treated the decision as an outrage. The kitchen had served people too weary to cook after work and those whose wages barely covered rent. Its sturdy tables had hosted both quiet meals and merry celebrations. Now a small notice announced an immediate farewell. Volunteers were wary of confronting the council, but a timid cook named Mei made a public plea: repair the building, she asked, rather than abandon the people who depended on it.","zh":"社区厨房关闭让全区沮丧。严厉的官员说破旧建筑不安全，愤慨而不安的人群认为决定令人愤怒。这里服务下班疲惫者，也服务工资仅够房租的人。坚固餐桌既承载安静晚餐，也见证欢乐聚会，如今小告示宣布立即告别。志愿者谨慎，不愿对抗议会，但胆怯的厨师梅公开恳求：修房子，而不要抛弃依靠它的人。"},{"en":"The debate exposed more than a building problem. An eloquent property developer offered a gorgeous replacement restaurant that most former visitors could never afford. A benevolent donor proposed emergency funding, but his jealous business partner dismissed the guests as pathetic. Mei felt numb at this contrast. Expressions of compassion were easy; practical support was harder. She disliked the hypocrisy of praising community spirit while treating poverty with scorn. Her own ego also troubled her: she wanted to win the argument partly because she feared losing a place where people seemed to adore her cooking.","zh":"争论暴露的不只是建筑问题。能言善辩的开发商提出华丽替代餐厅，多数老顾客却负担不起。仁慈的捐助者愿意应急出资，嫉妒的生意伙伴则轻蔑地称顾客可悲。对比令梅麻木。表达同情容易，实际支持难。她厌恶赞扬社区精神却鄙视贫困的伪善，也反思自身自我：想赢，部分因为怕失去人们热爱她厨艺的地方。"},{"en":"At a hearing, the council chair adopted a cordial manner but asked questions that seemed designed to bewilder the volunteers. Mei avoided a hysterical response and presented bills, attendance records, and a discreet account of residents' needs. One speaker described a homeless man as a dumb troublemaker, and she asked the chair to pardon her interruption before challenging the label. There was no need to pity him, she argued, if pity meant denying his ability to contribute. Nor should a naughty child at dinner be treated like a wicked enemy. People needed rules, but also patient explanations and room to improve.","zh":"听证会上，主席态度热忱，提问却似乎有意让志愿者困惑。梅避免歇斯底里，提交账单、出席记录，并谨慎说明居民需求。一人称无家可归者是愚蠢的麻烦制造者，她先请主席原谅打断，再质疑标签。如果同情意味着否定其贡献能力，就不必如此同情他。淘气的孩子也不是邪恶敌人。人们需要规则，也需要耐心解释与改进空间。"},{"en":"The testimony included an amiable retired nurse who called her husband darling even after forty years of marriage. She explained how shared dinners had eased her anguish following his illness. Another visitor described the fright of entering the kitchen alone, followed by relief when someone welcomed him. Such accounts could amaze officials accustomed to statistics, but Mei refused to claim that the service was flawless. There had been a grim dispute over alcohol and one ruthless attempt to steal donated funds. The kitchen also hosted a nurse who explained sexual health, including the risks of unprotected intercourse. Honest discussion, rather than cunning publicity, was essential to trust.","zh":"证词中，亲切的退休护士结婚四十年仍叫丈夫“亲爱的”，她说共同晚餐缓解了丈夫病后自己的痛苦。另一位访客讲述独自进门的惊恐，以及受欢迎后的释然。这些经历让习惯统计数据的官员惊讶，但梅不宣称服务无缺陷：曾有严重酒精纠纷，也有人无情盗取善款。厨房还请护士讲解性健康，包括无保护性行为的风险。信任需要诚实讨论，而非狡猾宣传。"},{"en":"The final agreement allowed repairs and a temporary kitchen nearby. It was not a jolly ending to every difficulty, and a careless headline might still appal someone looking only for scandal. Nevertheless, the volunteers returned with renewed zeal. Mei understood that a community was not a riddle solved by separating admirable people from everyone else. It was an arrangement that helped imperfect people share responsibilities. Calling an opponent an idiot might offer brief satisfaction, but listening could reveal that even hostile parties wanted a safer district. The strongest case for the kitchen was that it made such ordinary cooperation possible.","zh":"最终协议允许维修，并在附近设置临时厨房。这不意味着所有困难都有快乐结局，草率标题仍可能吓坏只寻找丑闻的人，但志愿者重燃热情。梅懂得，社区不是把优秀者与其余人分开就能破解的谜，而是帮助不完美的人共同负责的安排。骂对手白痴也许暂时痛快，聆听却可能发现敌对双方都希望地区更安全。厨房最有力的价值，在于促成这种日常合作。"}],"previous":58,"next":60});
